//
// File:    std/compilefail_test.skink
// Purpose: Negative-compilation harness. Every snippet in
//          std/compilefail/*.skink MUST fail to compile, and the
//          compiler's output must contain the substring named by the
//          snippet's first-line `// expect: <text>` marker. This is the
//          only suite that verifies malformed and semantically invalid
//          programs are rejected — positive tests cannot cover that.
//          Snippets guard: comp_error.md #35 (fixed arrays), #76
//          (for-in over int), #77 (&m[k]), #79 (method values),
//          #81 (struct ==), plus general diagnostic quality.
